        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gabe Saporta, John S. Hall\n- Bands: Cobra Starship, King Missile\n- Songs: \"Snakes on a Plane (Bring It)\"\n- Places: New York City, New York\n\nFacts:\n- John S. Hall was born as John Charles Hall on September 2, 1960.\n- John S. Hall is an American poet, author, singer, and lawyer.\n- John S. Hall co-founded the avant-garde band King Missile in 1986 and has led it in various incarnations since then.\n- Gabe Saporta was born on October 11, 1979.\n- Gabe Saporta is a Uruguayan-American musician and entrepreneur.\n- Cobra Starship was created by former Midtown bassist and lead vocalist Gabe Saporta in 2006 in New York City, New York.\n- Cobra Starship was an American dance-pop band.\n- \"Snakes on a Plane (Bring It)\" was the debut single by Cobra Starship.\n- \"Snakes on a Plane (Bring It)\" was also referred to as \"Bring It (Snakes on a Plane)\" and was released in 2006 from the soundtrack album \"Snakes on a Plane.\"",
